  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\r39FA101 A received on 17/11/2025, 39FA104 A, 39FA209 A, DESIGN AND ACCESS STATEMENT    \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen/dinning room and lounge shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The rear garden of the site must be accessible and usable at all times by all future occupiers for as long as the property remains in C4 Use. \r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accommodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan.\r",
    "Within six months of the granting of planning permission, cycle parking must be provided in compliance with the following criteria: and maintained thereafter to the satisfcation of the Local Planning Authority:\r\r-provision of a minimum of six long stay cycle parking spaces\r\r-in an accessible location: the access route to the store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike\r\r-to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gate (excluding the store door).\r\r-secured: with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob\r\r-fully enclosed: four walls and a roof\r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.\r"
  ],
